Conformance
Id	Clause
conformance.1	This module specification describes the module that tells Claude Code [CLAUDE-CODE] to record the raw API bodies and to run the conversion: it installs into the host claude-code. It is a module specification of the living-memory specification, and restates nothing that specification states.
conformance.2	The key words "MUST", "MUST NOT", "REQUIRED", "SHALL", "SHALL NOT", "SHOULD", "SHOULD NOT", "RECOMMENDED", "NOT RECOMMENDED", "MAY", and "OPTIONAL" in this specification are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 [BCP14] when, and only when, they appear in all capitals, as shown here.
conformance.3	The Rules are normative. Each rule states one requirement, and its Id names what it governs and the requirement's number: install, the change; capture, the recording; folder, where it is kept; hooks, the conversion and the context; context, what Claude is told. This specification has no optional features.
Rules
Id	Rule
install.1	The module MUST name its host, claude-code.
install.2	The module MUST state the change it makes before it is made: the folder it creates, the variable it sets and what that records, whether the request and response files are kept, and the three hooks it adds.
install.3	The module MUST write the user settings adding to what they hold: the capture variable, a Stop hook, a SessionStart hook and a UserPromptSubmit hook, not adding a matcher group they hold already, and replacing each group it added before, one whose command hook runs living-memory on the recording's folder, where it stands; settings files are strict JSON [CLAUDE-CODE].
install.4	The settings file MUST be replaced whole, written beside its name and renamed onto it.
install.5	The request and response files are spent once converted (raw_api_bodies.mtsv › recording.6). The module MUST ask whether to keep them, No by default; kept, each hook runs living-memory with --keep-files, the name GNU's table of long options gives to keeping files a program would otherwise remove [GNU].
capture.1	OTEL_LOG_RAW_API_BODIES set to file:<dir> writes the full Messages API request and response of each call, untruncated, under <dir>, and implies consent to everything OTEL_LOG_USER_PROMPTS, OTEL_LOG_TOOL_DETAILS and OTEL_LOG_TOOL_CONTENT would reveal [CLAUDE-CODE]. The module MUST set it to file: and the recording's folder, in the settings file's env, which sets environment variables for every session [CLAUDE-CODE].
capture.2	The variable is set in the shell, user settings or managed settings, and ignored in project and local settings; the user settings file is ~/.claude/settings.json, in every project, and CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR keeps the home-directory files somewhere else [CLAUDE-CODE]. The module MUST write the user settings file, settings.json in CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR where it is set, else in ~/.claude.
capture.3	A feature that reads its variables once at startup, as OpenTelemetry monitoring does, keeps its startup values until Claude Code is relaunched [CLAUDE-CODE]; the module MUST state that the recording begins with the next session.
folder.1	User data files are kept under $XDG_DATA_HOME, an absolute path, else ~/.local/share, on Linux [XDG-BASEDIR], and under ~/Library/Application Support on macOS [APPLE-FS]; a directory that does not exist is created with permission 0700 [XDG-BASEDIR]. The module MUST create the recording's folder there.
folder.2	The command does not run on Windows, which has no POSIX file lock, so the module MUST refuse to install there.
folder.3	The recording's folder MUST be living-memory, the application's name [PLATFORMDIRS], then anthropic/claude_code/raw_api_bodies, the path of the module that reads it, under the data directory.
hooks.1	Hooks are defined in JSON settings files, in three levels: a hook event, its matcher groups, and each group's hook handlers; a group whose matcher is omitted activates on every occurrence of its event; a command hook with args runs in exec form, with no shell [CLAUDE-CODE]. Each group the module adds MUST have no matcher and one command hook in exec form.
hooks.2	Stop runs when the main agent has finished responding, and a command hook with async true runs in the background [CLAUDE-CODE]; the Stop hook MUST run living-memory on the recording's folder in the background.
hooks.3	Events fire per session, SessionStart, and per turn, UserPromptSubmit, and from both plain-text stdout on exit 0 is added as context [CLAUDE-CODE]. The SessionStart and the UserPromptSubmit hook MUST each run living-memory --add-context=claude-code on the recording's folder, "add context" being the host's own word for the act [CLAUDE-CODE], which converts what is new, then prints the context.
hooks.4	Exit code 2 is a blocking error: from UserPromptSubmit it blocks prompt processing and erases the prompt [CLAUDE-CODE]. Run with --add-context, the command MUST exit with status 1 on any failure, which is a non-blocking error shown as a hook error notice [CLAUDE-CODE], and never with status 2.
hooks.5	A format named with -f/--from is not guessed [PANDOC]. Each hook MUST run living-memory with --from=anthropic/claude_code/raw_api_bodies, the path of the module that reads the recording (folder.3), so that a folder without index.jsonl is read by it (raw_api_bodies.mtsv › recording.8).
context.1	Added context is for the current state, written as factual statements, and saved in the transcript; SessionStart fires on startup, resume, clear, compact and fork [CLAUDE-CODE]. From SessionStart the context MUST be an MTSV file of these sheets, each named by the store's sheet and the column it is grouped by: store, the output's path and how many inputs it holds; raw_api_bodies by date, each date with how many sessions and requests; raw_api_bodies by session_id, query_source, the sessions of the session's date grouped as raw_api_bodies.mtsv › map.1 gives; and, where the session has an input, store by sheet, each of its sheet files with its sheet name and how many records, and store columns, each file's position and field name of its header.
context.2	On compaction the context the transcript held is replaced [CLAUDE-CODE]; from SessionStart with source compact the context MUST also hold raw_api_bodies not kept, the lineage of the session's latest request (raw_api_bodies.mtsv › map.2) grouped as map.1 gives.
context.3	Each fact is stored in one place [WICKHAM2014]. From UserPromptSubmit the context MUST hold only the session's requests the context has not yet given: raw_api_bodies, their records as the store holds them, and store by sheet, each sheet file their records are in, with the number of those records and the first and last of them, counted from 1; with none, nothing.
context.4	What the context has given MUST be kept beside the input's output as the number of its requests given, each SessionStart giving them all.
context.5	Added context is capped at 10,000 characters, and over it Claude is given its path and a preview alone [CLAUDE-CODE]. Where the context from UserPromptSubmit would pass the cap, its raw_api_bodies MUST be given as the groups raw_api_bodies.mtsv › map.1 gives of them, named raw_api_bodies by session_id, query_source.
